{"lauren:What evidence would tell us that the staggered schedule is fair?":"362ff9fec27f26553ee825c7bdcf25953ef5f727409157f2b5f9cdafd5566a4d","siren:A library proposes opening its study room to community groups after six. Students worry about noise during exams. Group organisers say a full ban would exclude people who cannot meet earlier. A separate entrance is available, but sound insulation has not been tested.":"0f08430706683a9adce97bbce05b5263071909014914f44558f329287be53a33","lauren:We only take cash. Do you still want the notebook?":"f1aaaf546a4da16636e40022330035d7aa69f223f27a0cf5f1e13a1044e628d8","lauren:Would you mind repeating that?":"e6ad4ff3adfd29f6717db8815eee0dd5ab135fad775a95cb186c65b5dcd0ba3d","lauren:The British editor kept honour, while the American editor used honor; both spellings were appropriate for their audiences.":"491df5ae912037d29255435edc58242aec6f820f22b21a6a7592e2e451fbb483","lauren:We should try that new board game, wanna join?":"ec5f5de48dc48a13eecd499515bb5812cddb1b258a12ef5439ebfdc83b683f72","lauren:You should read this novel; its character development is truly compelling.":"1baf8ae05f79473d6784130a979a6d6301712d26d61e8d0141a746b8df024a61"}